---
<Site title="Public information"><PageHeader title="Find reliable local information" eyebrow="Public information" description="Use a dated notice from the authority responsible for your place and water system. The right source differs by issue." /><section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Weather and farming</h3><p>Check the issue date, district and crop stage on an official forecast or agromet advisory before acting on it.</p><a href="https://mausam.imd.gov.in/imd_latest/contents/agromet/advisory/blocalmain.php">IMD agromet bulletins ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Supply interruption</h3><p>Use your verified local utility or panchayat notice. Record the date, area and reported response if you raise an issue collectively.</p><a href={url('/response/')}>How public actions are tracked ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Water quality</h3><p>Consult current local water-quality advisories and the responsible public-health authority. A rainfall map or distant test cannot establish whether your tap is safe.</p><a href="https://jaljeevanmission.gov.in/sites/default/files/guideline/WQMS-Framework.pdf">JJM quality framework ↗</a></article></div><div class="note" style="margin-top:3rem"><strong>Local contacts are not listed yet</strong><p>We have not verified a nationwide contact number or place-specific utility directory. The source catalogue records the work still needed.</p></div></div></section></Site>
